-<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy">
-    <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
-    <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+<LegalLayout title="Privacy Notice">
+    <p>The DevTools Times is a demonstration news site. You can read articles and use search without creating an account. Please use made-up account details and a password you do not use anywhere else.</p>
+
+    <h2>Account forms: what is sent and why</h2>
+    <p>Sign-up asks only for a username and password to create a demo account. Sign-in asks for the same details to check your credentials. A pseudonym is enough; neither form requests your real name, email, phone number or other profile information.</p>
+    <p>Only when you submit a form, your browser sends those two fields over HTTPS to the external account service at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code>, using <code>/times_cdn/api/register</code> for sign-up or <code>/times_cdn/api/login</code> for sign-in. The service also receives your IP address and browser request information. The requests omit cookies and referrer information.</p>
+    <p>The forms do not save credentials or returned tokens in local storage, session storage or cookies. Password fields are cleared after each request finishes, including failed requests. Your browser or password manager may separately offer to save credentials under your own settings. Successful sign-in checks credentials with the demo service; it does not establish a signed-in session on this site.</p>
+
+    <h2>Account retention and deletion</h2>
+    <p>The external account service handles account records. This site's source does not specify that service's retention period, password-storage safeguards or a way to access, correct or delete account records. The site currently has no account-management or deletion flow. Do not submit personal or reusable credentials. If you do not want to send data to that service, continue reading without an account.</p>
+
+    <h2>Third-party resources</h2>
+    <p>The shared layout does not load third-party analytics, advertising scripts or remote fonts. Account pages use first-party resources until you submit the form. Some articles and media links elsewhere on the site reference external image or media providers; those providers receive network information when your browser requests their resources. The site sets a no-referrer policy to avoid sending the referring page's address.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading lists and demo features</h2>
+    <p>The reading-list feature is designed to store article identifiers in a server-side session when you choose to save or remove an article. Where sessions are configured, the browser uses a session cookie to associate requests with that list. Reading the site alone does not initialize an empty reading list. This is separate from the demo account service. Some demonstration articles also include feature-specific requests or cookies.</p>
+
+    <h2>Browser permissions and hosting</h2>
+    <p>The site disables camera, microphone, location, motion-sensor and advertising-topics access through its document permissions policy. The hosting provider necessarily receives connection information such as your IP address and requested URL. This repository does not establish the provider's log retention settings.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
